WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.734
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.734
and comedian you know
from "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:07.234
which premieres
this Saturday on NBC and Peacock

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:10.767
with host Pete Davidson
and musical guest Ice Spice.

00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:13.501
He also stars in
"Dicks: The Musical,"

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:16.167
which is in select theaters
now and nationwide October 20th.

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.267
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.100
our very good friend Bowen Yang,
everybody.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.200
♪♪

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:34.000
♪♪

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.701
Welcome back.
-Thank you. Thanks, Seth.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.167
-You have not just "SNL."

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.968
You have one of my favorite
podcasts, "Las Culturistas."

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.400
-Oh, my goodness.
-And you took it on --

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
There we go. Give it up.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.734
-You know, someone might
be on it soon.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.834
-I can't wait.
You took it to Europe.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:53.434
You did live shows in London
and Berlin and Amsterdam.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:54.634
-Yes, yes.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.434
Those are the big
expat markets, apparently.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:59.534
-Yeah.
-It was really fun.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:01.200
-We talked about Amsterdam.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.567
I was doing shows
in Amsterdam in the summer.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.667
I went back to Boom Chicago,

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.100
which is the theater
I used to work at.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.234
And it's actually where
you did your live podcast.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.701
-That's right, that's right.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.133
-Did you do anything fun in
Amsterdam while you were there?

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:11.934
-We just walked the canals.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:14.434
We took a boat,
and I love Amsterdam.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:17.100
I went twice this summer.
I -- My only issue with it

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.701
is that it's tough
when you combine a city --

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:24.167
when you combine weed
with bicycles.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.167
I feel like it's a recipe
for disaster.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.467
Crossing the street
is really scary.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:30.734
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.467
It is not -- So you even --

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.267
You're not even saying
like being on a bicycle,

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:36.968
just being stoned
on foot is scary

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.868
because there's so many
bicycles.

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:40.434
-You don't have to be
the person who's stoned.

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.868
You might be next
to a stoned person,

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.000
and then they're the ones
who, like, causes a big,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.534
like 10-person pileup
or something.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.267
-A bike pileup.
-A bike pileup.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.701
-It is. I will say,
you have to do a lot wrong

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:53.934
for a car to come near you
on a bicycle in Amsterdam.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.200
Like, the cars
are so aware of the bikes,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.400
and that is very nice.
But I will say on foot,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.267
sometimes you'll just walk
right into the path.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.300
-That's right, that's right.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.801
-And the Dutch people
are very --

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:05.434
I love them very much.
They are cold and unforgiving.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.801
-But that said with love.
-Yes.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.133
Did you go to did you go
to any museums?

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:15.801
-I did. The hot ticket
is the Van Gogh Museum,

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.033
and concierge in my hotel

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:18.968
was very, very good
about getting me tickets.

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.234
And he did say to me,

00:02:21.234 --> 00:02:25.501
"This is harder than getting
Taylor Swift tickets."

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.834
And I said,
"That can't be true."

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:32.534
There's no way that's true."
And, like, you know,

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.734
there aren't, like, teen girls
fighting me for it,

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.467
so it's fine.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:40.234
-There was I feel like a fight
to get into the Lincoln Center,

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.434
Las Culturistas Awards.
-Yes.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:44.067
-You did that this --
Was it this summer?

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.300
-It was this summer, yes.
-And so one of our producers,

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.334
Henry, was there, and he said
there was literally two loops

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:50.701
around the block to get in.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.400
-Yeah, that's pretty crazy.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.501
It was a free show.
So that explains it.

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:55.667
-Yeah. Yeah. Free show.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.467
But again, you were
giving out awards

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.033
and they were
the culture awards.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:02:59.968
-That's right.
-And for people

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:01.133
who don't know the podcast,

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.200
you kind of give out
the sort of awards

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.300
that I feel like are overlooked

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.868
by a lot of
the main award shows.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.200
-Absolutely.
-Like, for example,

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.434
you gave out the the Chris Award
for Most Timeless Name.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.901
-Most Timeless Name.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:17.400
-The nominees were John,
Jess, George, Mark and Doja.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.567
-Yeah, Doja. Doja Cat. Pretty
timeless name, I would say.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.400
She did not win.
-Do you remember who won?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.634
-Oh, this is a quiz.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.234
-No, I didn't mean
to make it a quiz.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:27.367
-That's okay.
-I was going to say it.

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:28.667
-Please.
-Jess.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.934
-Jess.
-And why do you think --

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:32.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.267
-I don't know.

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:36.367
This is literally
on a spreadsheet

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:39.734
and we just, like,
change the cell color to blue.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.601
We're like, "Yeah, this one.
Let's crown it."

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.434
-This is my favorite --
Free Willy Award

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:46.934
for Animal Achievement,
Jenny the donkey.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.767
-Oh, from
"Banshees of Inisherin."

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.501
-Had a big year.
Mickey Mouse.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.601
Always good year.
-Big year for Mickey.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.834
-The cast
of "The Secret Life of Pets,"

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.534
which I feel like
came out a while ago.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:04:00.667
-Right.
But look, they've achieved.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:04.234
-And then the winner
was tortoises, all.

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:07.234
-All tortoises.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.133
-I mean, it does --
it makes sense

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:10.701
people were lined
around the block.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.000
-Yes. You want to know.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.167
You want to know.
There were big upsets.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.100
I mean, Jenny the donkey
is probably really upset.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.033
-I know. Jenny looked
at the nominees and was like,

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:20.234
"It's my year."
-"It's my year," but no.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.734
-The good news for Jenny is
based on

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:24.033
"The Secret Life of Pets" cast,

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.467
Jenny might get nominated
10 years from now.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:27.734
-Definitely, definitely.

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:28.767
-Don't give up.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.334
-If Colin Farrell
can make a comeback,

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:32.367
so can Jenny.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.300
Pete Davidson
is hosting this week.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.100
-Yes!
-Now that must be the first time

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.868
someone you worked with
has come back to host.

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:40.100
Is that --
-Yeah. That's true.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.968
-That's a real passage of time.
I think maybe --

00:04:42.968 --> 00:04:44.400
Well, probably for me
it was Will Ferrell.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.901
Will Ferrell came back to host
and I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:04:45.901 --> 00:04:47.234
We were cast members together."

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:50.033
And so what has it been like
for you with Pete back?

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:51.567
-It's been great.
It's so nice.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:54.434
It's just nice to like have the
shorthand already with someone.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:55.467
-Yeah.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:56.567
-And we did our read-through
yesterday

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:59.033
and he -- we read
about like 35 sketches.

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:02.601
Right? And I think at the half,
at the break he said,

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.734
"This is more sketches
than I've been in

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.667
than my eight years
at this show."

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.501
We were like,
"Maybe you're right."

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:11.968
-Five months out of the office.

00:05:11.968 --> 00:05:14.734
Now, I guess you got a little --
you lost some shows on

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.400
the back end of the season,

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.167
but it was the summer
when people are away.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.067
But, you know,
it was abbreviated year,

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:21.434
and maybe people left
a little bit quicker

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:22.934
than they would have.
What was the scene

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.534
like as everybody
went back to their offices?

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.267
-It was smelly.
-Yeah.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:29.067
-It was smelly
because five months,

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:34.000
guess what's in the fridges.
Our takeout food from May.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.467
-Yeah.
-And yeah, I think,

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:40.834
I still have a fruit cup
in my fridge down the hall

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:45.300
that has the whitest and
blackest mold I've ever seen.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.701
-That's amazing.
-That's amazing.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.667
-You know what? You don't just
do comedy, you do science.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.367
And that's what I've always
respected about you.

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:52.067
I want to talk about
"Dicks: The Musical."

00:05:52.067 --> 00:05:54.300
We'll be right back with more
from Bowen Yang.

